Z||000000||Tfeldt||02-12-2000||04:23 PM||||I have an 87 V6 GT that idles OK for a while, then all of a sudden it will increse several hundred RPM, then back down again.  It will do this over and over again.  Could it be a bad IAC Valve (it was just replaced a year ago)?  I would also like to know what the screw is on the Throttle body does, and where and how it should be adjusted. <BR>Thanx.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-12-2000||09:55 PM||||A baseline needs to be established, a complete tuneup, emissions check, and compression test.  Get a mechanic that doesn't mind being watched, and maybe even talks to himself as he works.  This will familiarize you with procedures and adjustments, pinpoint where this particular problem is coming from, and give you valuable future reference material.  And it will be expensive.  <BR>Elimiate as many of the above sources of probs that you can by yourself and give results to the forum, somebody will be sure to tell where to go.  Next, that is.  <BR>Cheaper this way but you gots to find reference books and eliminate the first 90 percent of causes yourself.||||reg||1
